1
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:07,132
<i>'Bi.</i>

2
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:12,303
<i>What?</i>

3
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:14,014
<i>There's something I need you to do.</i>

4
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:19,686
<i>Ms. Talia?</i>

5
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:21,479
<i>- Yes?</i>
<i>- Ms. Talia, hi.</i>

6
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:23,022
<i>Do you remember me?</i>

7
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,691
- <i>I know that the reason--</i>
- [ENGINE ROARING]

8
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:26,693
- <i>Hey! Hey!</i>
- [TALIA GASPS]

9
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:27,902
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

10
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,487
[TALIA] <i>Oh! Oh my God!</i>

11
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:31,281
[GASPS]<i> Are you okay?</i>

12
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:32,741
<i>Oh my goodness!</i>

13
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:34,367
<i>- Oh…</i>
- [BEA GRUNTS]

14
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:36,036
<i>You're wounded!</i>

15
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,746
[SOFT GROAN] <i>I'm okay, ma'am.</i>

16
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,790
<i>- Are you okay?</i>
<i>- Yes. Here's your bag.</i>

17
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,417
<i>- Hi!</i>
- [HR OFFICER] <i>Hi.</i>

18
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,878
<i>You didn't call me.</i>

19
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:46,504
<i>Never mind, that's okay.</i>

20
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,471
[CALOY] <i>Sorry.</i>

21
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,349
<i>I was too rough, so you got dragged.</i>

22
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:01,686
<i>It's fine. It made our act</i>
<i>even more convincing.</i>

23
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:04,272
<i>Ms. Talia really felt bad for me.</i>

24
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,525
- [MARJ] <i>I think it's perfect.</i>
<i>- Guys?</i>

25
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,236
<i>So, I have good news.</i>

26
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:13,573
<i>I have a potential sponsor,</i>

27
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>and it's…</i>

28
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:18,328
<i>Talia & Co., the jewelry brand!</i>

29
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:19,287
[GIGGLES]

30
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,288
<i>Wow!</i>

31
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:22,248
<i>They just have one request, though.</i>

32
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>Okay…</i>

33
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:26,252
[TALIA] <i>So we are continuing this campaign</i>

34
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,838
<i>with our next partner,</i>

35
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:32,342
<i>Billy Cariño of LoveList.</i>

36
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:36,763
<i>She is the perfect next partner for us.</i>

37
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:39,724
<i>They want you to wear this</i>
<i>to the awards night.</i>

38
00:01:40,391 --> 00:01:43,144
<i>This necklace costs 30 million.</i>

39
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:46,564
[BILLY] <i>Wow.</i>

40
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:47,982
[CHARM] <i>It's beautiful!</i>

41
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:51,986
[TALIA] <i>What do you think?</i>
<i>It's a great idea, right?</i>

42
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:53,488
<i>What do you think?</i>

43
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,074
<i>- What do you think?</i>
<i>- Sounds great!</i>

44
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:57,117
<i>Yes!</i>

45
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:59,285
<i>Uh, Bea?</i>

46
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:01,496
<i>- Ma'am?</i>
- [TALIA] <i>Yes?</i>

47
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:04,040
<i>Yes, I agree with you, Ms. Talia!</i>

48
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,375
<i>Very good.</i>

49
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:09,629
<i>I think she'll make a wonderful partner</i>
<i>for our event.</i>

50
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:15,468
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

51
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,554
[JORDAN SIGHS]

52
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:18,805
Dude, I'm sorry.

53
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:21,599
I searched every corner of the Net.

54
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:22,559
Mm-hmm.

55
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:25,687
But I couldn't find anything
about Bea's father

56
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:27,272
or her family.

57
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:29,774
Well,

58
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:33,194
It's hard to find someone
who doesn't want to be found.

59
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,322
Maybe you're right.

60
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:38,950
Maybe they have prior criminal records.

61
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:41,202
But I'm sorry, dude…

62
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,662
I know you don't--

63
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:43,913
That's enough apologies.

64
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:46,374
- Stop it.
- What?

65
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,751
Come on, stop it!

66
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:51,963
Thank you for taking the time
to look for Bea's father.

67
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:53,882
And don't worry.

68
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:58,011
I already have a plan for Bea and Caloy.

69
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:00,430
Really?

70
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:01,848
Mm-hmm.

71
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:06,811
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:07,854
Now go away.

73
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:09,856
[BILLY GIGGLES]

74
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,738
We hit the jackpot with this!

75
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:18,197
But more importantly,

76
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:21,367
this will be a huge blow to Billy!

77
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,121
Okay.

78
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:28,416
Just tell me when and where.

79
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:32,587
I'll do anything for you.

80
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,172
It's for us.

81
00:03:35,381 --> 00:03:36,341
I'll hang up now.

82
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:43,431
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:51,564
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:04:31,437 --> 00:04:35,566
IF YOU EVER NEED HELP, I'M HERE.

85
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:39,988
- Look at that beautiful smile!
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]

86
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,615
I just saw a funny meme.

87
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:44,409
- Really?
- Yes.

88
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:46,953
Okay. A meme from Brandon?

89
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:50,873
What? No. You're so silly!

90
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,126
- You know what, Auntie Pres?
- What?

91
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:54,919
Happiness looks good on you.

92
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,421
I hope you always stay happy.

93
00:04:56,504 --> 00:05:00,591
Mm-hmm. I hope you do too.

94
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:04,804
I hope you stay happy
despite all the challenges you're facing.

95
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:07,932
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,058
I can handle it.

97
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:13,271
Especially since I have people
around me who help me.

98
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:22,071
<i>- Come with me. Let's go.</i>
<i>- Brandon, that hurts!</i>

99
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,489
<i>Bro.</i>

100
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,241
<i>Bro.</i>

101
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:27,744
<i>Don't force her to come</i>
<i>if she doesn't want to.</i>

102
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:31,748
<i>You should go.</i>

103
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,917
<i>I'll call security if you don't.</i>

104
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,837
<i>Brandon, please just leave.</i>

105
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,423
<i>- I can fight you, you know?</i>
<i>- Hey! Oliver!</i>

106
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:41,424
<i>Break it up!</i>

107
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,760
<i>Go back to your classroom.</i>

108
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:46,721
<i>What are you all looking at?</i>

109
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,139
<i>Go back to your classrooms.</i>

110
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,559
- That's right.
- Mm.

111
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:58,649
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,953
<i>- ♪ Baby, I… ♪</i>
- [GUITAR STRUMMING]

113
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:16,375
[HUMMING]

114
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,795
[JORDAN] Sorry. I'll do it again. Ready?

115
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:25,760
<i>♪ You matter more to me than being right ♪</i>

116
00:06:25,843 --> 00:06:30,848
<i>♪ Baby, I won't be long ♪</i>

117
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:34,852
<i>♪ I'll be back by the end of the song ♪</i>

118
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:41,984
What do you think?

119
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,279
It's okay, boss,

120
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:48,199
but it lacks emotion.

121
00:06:48,282 --> 00:06:51,035
It's missing that emotional punch.

122
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:54,580
I agree, boss. How about this?

123
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:59,794
Just imagine you're singing
to the love of your life.

124
00:06:59,877 --> 00:07:01,462
That's it.

125
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,756
You know, Robbie is right.

126
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,550
Do it this way.

127
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:07,426
Pretend you still love me.

128
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,929
Go on. One more time.

129
00:07:10,012 --> 00:07:11,472
No, it's good enough.

130
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:13,099
Jordan…

131
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:17,979
The organizer of the PBS Executive
Circle Awards is a friend of mine.

132
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:21,023
I recommended you because I know you.

133
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:24,819
When you sing, you give us all the feels.

134
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:27,113
But why do you seem so distracted today?

135
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:28,531
Because of Billy.

136
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:31,617
What?

137
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:37,415
I mean, because you're dealing
with Billy's problems.

138
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:41,461
Because it also affects LoveList.

139
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:42,670
I know that.

140
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,214
Okay, I'm sorry.

141
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,136
Go. One more time.

142
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:52,805
- Go! Yes!
- Let's go.

143
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:54,807
- [ROBBIE] Let's go!
- [VALERIE] Whoo!

144
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:56,767
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

145
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:10,823
<i>♪ Can we take a rest? ♪</i>

146
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,118
So? How does it look?

147
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,953
[CHARM] Wow, it's so pretty!

148
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:19,290
- It's so pretty, right?
- Definitely worth 30 million!

149
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:22,084
Keep your eyes on it later, okay?
We can't afford to lose it.

150
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:25,671
Diamond represents power, so you go, girl!

151
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:29,175
- [CHARM] It's so pretty and shiny.
- Yeah, it looks good on you.

152
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,178
But, you know,
I feel like it would look better on me.

153
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:35,681
Because I have a longer neck
and I'm paler than you.

154
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:37,141
[CHUCKLING AWKWARDLY]

155
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:38,476
- You're so funny.
- You know what?

156
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:41,771
You should try tourmaline
to attract good vibes.

157
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:42,688
I agree.

158
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,982
- Yours is pretty, too.
- [MARJ] You already have one.

159
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,400
So funny. It looks good.

160
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,903
You know, guys,
I think we should get some coffee.

161
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:50,821
The event isn't until later. Come on.

162
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:52,615
- [MARJ] Right.
- [CHARM] Oh, perfect.

163
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:55,660
Ralph is downstairs.
Let's ask him to treat us.

164
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:56,994
- Okay. Let's go.
- Wait, wait.

165
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,663
What about the necklace?

166
00:08:58,746 --> 00:08:59,830
[VALERIE] I'll…

167
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,082
I got it.

168
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:02,291
- [MARJ] Okay.
- Hold on.

169
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,584
- Keep it safe.
- Don't lose it.

170
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:04,835
Yes.

171
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,963
- Billy, be careful with it.
- Go. Keep it safe.

172
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,798
- [BILLY] Yes!
- It's expensive.

173
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:14,720
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:31,362
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:40,079
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

176
00:09:54,885 --> 00:10:01,058
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

177
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:08,232
[CARS HONKING IN DISTANCE]

178
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:12,361
I hope our luck continues.

179
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:17,158
Our numbers are doing good,
thanks to Happily Ever After!

180
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:18,909
It's not just luck, Toni.

181
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:20,995
We worked hard for all of this.

182
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:23,456
My investment in LoveList was worth it.

183
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:25,333
- So, cheers to that.
- [TONI] Yes!

184
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:27,585
[CHARM] Well, hopefully,
your mom feels the same way.

185
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:31,964
So she can be assured that
your money didn't go to waste.

186
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:35,092
Why? It's your money anyway, Ralph, right?

187
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:36,969
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,095
Um…

189
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:40,014
Well, in their family,

190
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:42,433
one person's money is everyone's money.

191
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:45,728
They're a big corporation, so technically,

192
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:49,815
the money invested in us
is the family's company money.

193
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:55,112
Is that a bad thing?

194
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,365
Definitely bad.

195
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,826
I mean, if you actually
want to get married

196
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,578
and lead your own home one day.

197
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:06,540
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

198
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,583
See?

199
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,336
Look at how obvious it is, babe.

200
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:13,214
Even at this point, you can't make
decisions completely on your own.

201
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:16,008
It's as if your umbilical cord
is still tied to your family,

202
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,468
especially to your mother.

203
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:20,012
Well, maybe they're just
looking out for me.

204
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,098
[CHARM] Looking out for you? Why?

205
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,850
Am I a danger to you, huh?

206
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:27,103
[SCOFFS] Here we go again.

207
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,772
- [GLASS CLINKS]
- Ralph, Charm.

208
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:31,232
We keep going in circles.

209
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:32,608
- [RALPH SCOFFS]
- [CHAIR SCRAPING]

210
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,863
Guys, excuse me.

211
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,156
[CHARM] Ralph!

212
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,577
- [RALPH SCOFFS]
- Ralph!

213
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:45,371
[RALPH] Sorry, bro.

214
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:49,125
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

215
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:50,334
Oh my.

216
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,879
Their lover's quarrel came
at the wrong time.

217
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,006
I know, right?

218
00:11:56,590 --> 00:12:03,055
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

219
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:12,022
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

220
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:30,332
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

221
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,880
Water, water. Hmmm…

222
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:38,048
Two towels.

223
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:41,594
And two tissues.

224
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,972
Okay, this will be fine.

225
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:46,223
Hey, handsome.

226
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:48,225
Yes, sir?

227
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:50,811
I saw you earlier.

228
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:52,813
What about it?

229
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,398
Would you like to be famous?

230
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:56,942
But, sir, I might get…

231
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:01,071
Here, call me later. Take my number.

232
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,114
Here, when you get home.

233
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,492
But, sir, I might get fired for that.

234
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:05,910
I'll just slide it into your pocket.

235
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,495
Oh, okay, okay, sir.

236
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,748
- I might get fired, sir.
- Open it later.

237
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,000
[CHUCKLES] You're quite the macho guy.

238
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:15,002
- Okay. Thank you, sir.
- Call me, okay?

239
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,004
[HOUSEKEEPER] Housekeeping!

240
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:23,135
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:27,556
[PHONE RINGING]

242
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,228
Hello.

243
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,731
Okay.

244
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:36,649
Thank you.

245
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:40,319
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

246
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:41,445
[PHONE THUDDING]

247
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:48,327
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

248
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:53,582
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,459
[SOFT THUDDING]

250
00:13:59,046 --> 00:13:59,964
[SOFT THUD]

251
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,592
[DOOR CREAKING OPEN]

252
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:09,223
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

253
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:17,648
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:33,289
[JORDAN, CALOY GRUNTING]

255
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,832
- Dude!
- Get off me!

256
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,084
- [PEPPER SPRAY HISSES]
- [SCREAMS]

257
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:38,711
[BILLY] Jordan! The necklace!

258
00:14:39,336 --> 00:14:41,088
- Go, go, go!
- [BILLY] Run!

259
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:43,424
- [CALOY] Get back here!
- Go!

260
00:14:43,507 --> 00:14:44,884
I'll kill both of you!

261
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:46,719
- [BILLY] Jordan, let's go!
- Give me the necklace!

262
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:48,512
- [CALOY GRUNTS]
- [JORDAN] Stay back. Stay back.

263
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,222
[CALOY BREATHING HEAVILY]

264
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,016
Give me back the necklace,
or I'll kill you.

265
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:53,893
- Put the knife down.
- Give it to me!

266
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:56,478
- I'll give it to you. Just don't--
- I'll kill you if you don't.

267
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,105
- Jordan!
- It's yours, it's yours.

268
00:14:58,188 --> 00:14:59,440
Give it to me!

269
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,525
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,027
- [DOOR CREAKS OPEN]
- Hands in the air!

271
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,529
[OFFICER 1] Hands in the air!
No sudden movements!

272
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:08,324
[OFFICER] Cuff him!
Don't make any sudden movements.

273
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:10,659
- [OFFICER 2] Let the knife go!
- [CALOY] Fine!

274
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:11,827
- [CALOY] There!
- Let it go!

275
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,162
[CALOY GRUNTING IN PAIN]

276
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:15,122
[CALOY BREATHING HEAVILY]

277
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:17,875
- [CALOY] I'll come back for you.
- [OFFICER] Don't do anything stupid.

278
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,169
[CHUCKLING] You set me up?

279
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:22,504
You set me up, huh?!

280
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:24,965
- [CALOY BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [OFFICER 1] Get out!

281
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:27,092
- Just wait until I get out.
- [OFFICERS GRUNT]

282
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:29,428
You didn't fight fair!

283
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:31,472
[OFFICER 2] Let's go! Come on!

284
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:38,187
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

285
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:40,147
Move!

286
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:42,107
Go! Move!

287
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,442
Stop resisting!

288
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:47,738
Stop resisting!

289
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:49,865
[GRUNTS] Move!

290
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:51,909
- Get inside! Go!
- [CALOY] Wait.

291
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,453
- Stop resisting!
- [CALOY] Hold on.

292
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:57,164
- Get in!
- [CALOY GRUNTS] Sir…

293
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:58,874
- [SIGHS]
- [OFFICER] Let's go!

294
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:03,963
Justice said "not today"
and karma handled it.

295
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:06,215
[POLICE SIREN WAILING]

296
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:09,468
Okay, that's it for today's meeting.
I'll see you again next week.

297
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:11,553
Ma'am, I'll take care of this.

298
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:16,934
See you! Take care!

299
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:28,779
Ms. Beatrice Mercado?

300
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:33,701
You need to come with us
to the police station now.

301
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:41,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:44,461
Well, your plan worked.

303
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:47,256
Because of you, Ms. Talia.

304
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:54,013
<i>I am not considering</i>
<i>Bea Mercado for the position,</i>

305
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,056
<i>especially with her track record.</i>

306
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,766
<i>- Mm-hm.</i>
<i>- But…</i>

307
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,477
<i>when I found out that her</i>
<i>case is involved with you,</i>

308
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,812
<i>I called you.</i>

309
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:03,981
<i>I'm worried about you, Billy.</i>

310
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:07,067
<i>Thank you, Ms. Talia.</i>

311
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:10,279
<i>She says the accusations</i>
<i>against her are not true.</i>

312
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:12,322
<i>- Mm.</i>
<i>- So…</i>

313
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,658
<i>I wanted to get your side of the story.</i>

314
00:17:18,078 --> 00:17:20,748
<i>There's only one thing</i>
<i>you need to know, Ms. Talia.</i>

315
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:25,419
<i>You can't trust Bea Mercado.</i>

316
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:28,881
<i>And I can prove that.</i>

317
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,133
<i>How?</i>

318
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,347
<i>I'll be needing your help.</i>

319
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:41,060
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

320
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:43,353
<i>Ever since we rolled out this campaign,</i>

321
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:45,898
<i>there has been an increase in</i>
<i>the number of our followers.</i>

322
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:48,734
<i>And of course, this translates into</i>

323
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:50,069
<i>sales!</i>

324
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,529
<i>So we are continuing this campaign</i>

325
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:55,115
<i>with our next partner,</i>

326
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:58,786
<i>Billy Cariño of LoveList.</i>

327
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:02,998
<i>She is the perfect next partner for us.</i>

328
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:06,043
<i>More than just having a big following</i>
<i>and being a businesswoman,</i>

329
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:08,003
<i>she is relevant.</i>

330
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:10,589
[BEA] <i>We hit the jackpot with this!</i>

331
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:12,132
<i>But more importantly,</i>

332
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:15,052
<i>this will be a huge blow to Billy!</i>

333
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:18,847
Good thing she took the bait.

334
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:20,641
Thank you.

335
00:18:20,724 --> 00:18:22,601
Billy, anything for you.

336
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:26,563
In fact, I should be the one to thank you.

337
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,982
You know that I almost gave up on love.

338
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:33,529
<i>I thought it was too late</i>
<i>for me to find someone.</i>

339
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:37,574
If not for LoveList and you,

340
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:41,286
maybe I would not have found my forever.

341
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,246
So…

342
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:44,373
thank you very much.

343
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:45,791
I have to go.

344
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:51,088
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:53,006
Happy anniversary, my love.

346
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:54,967
[GASPS] They're beautiful.

347
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:56,301
Of course.

348
00:18:57,302 --> 00:18:58,846
Thank you.

349
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,021
Okay.

350
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:21,535
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:19:35,757 --> 00:19:37,217
[BEA] <i>I don't care</i>
<i>about that Billy.</i>

352
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:39,178
<i>And most importantly,</i>
<i>I don't care about you.</i>

353
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:40,762
<i>'Bi, don't say that.</i>

354
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,556
[BEA] <i>Don't touch me!</i>

355
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:45,809
<i>I never asked him to do anything</i>
<i>because I don't even know him!</i>

356
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,644
[MARIELA] <i>When will you leave</i>
<i>my daughter alone?</i>

357
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:50,272
<i>Like I told you before,</i>

358
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:53,317
<i>it's your daughter</i>
<i>you need to talk to.</i>

359
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:56,486
<i>And we'll let the world know</i>
<i>that she's also a criminal.</i>

360
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:58,739
<i>Can you please talk</i>
<i>to your people?</i>

361
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:01,742
<i>Maybe they want to know</i>
<i>what a real criminal is.</i>

362
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:03,660
<i>Do you think</i>
<i>you're going to scare me?</i>

363
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:05,746
<i>Enjoy your freedom,</i>
<i>because it won't last long.</i>

364
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:08,332
<i>It's way past your 10-day deadline</i>
<i>with Boss Zandro.</i>

365
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,583
<i>Do you think I'm an idiot?</i>

366
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:12,169
[NURSE] <i>You're listed as</i>
<i>an emergency contact.</i>

367
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:14,463
<i>For patient Enrico Dominguez.</i>

368
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,672
<i>- That's your problem!</i>
<i>- Jordan!</i>

369
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:17,799
<i>My friend has nothing</i>
<i>to do with it, okay?!</i>

370
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,552
<i>All he's missing is a girlfriend.</i>
<i>We'll find one for him.</i>

371
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:25,933
<i>♪ Baby, I won't be long ♪</i>

372
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:34,274
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]
